Retarget the nvptx accelerator compiler at CUDA 13-supported ISAs.

gcc/config.gcc defaults an nvptx target to --with-arch=sm_52 and expands the
multilib set to nvptx_multilibs_default, also sm_52.  (gcc/configure.ac:1220
sets with_multilib_list=default when --with-multilib-list is not passed, so
the 'xdefault | xyes' branch -- not the empty one -- is what runs in a stock
build.)  CUDA 13 dropped every ISA below sm_80, so ptxas rejects sm_52 and
the accelerator build dies:

    ptxas fatal : Value 'sm_52' is not defined for option 'gpu-name'
    configure: error: cannot compute suffix of object files
    make[1]: *** [configure-target-libgcc] Error 1

Move both defaults up: --with-arch=sm_80, multilib default sm_89.  config.gcc
prepends $with_arch to the expanded multilib list and de-duplicates, so this
yields TM_MULTILIB_CONFIG "sm_80 sm_89" with default -march=sm_80 -- both
lanes built.

GCC 16 has no sm_90 ISA: nvptx-sm.def tops out at sm_89 and nvptx.opt maps
-march=sm_90/sm_90a/sm_100 onto misa=sm_89, so sm_89 *is* the Hopper lane.
ptxas runs a `.target sm_XY` image on any sm_MN with MN >= XY, so sm_80
covers A100 and sm_89 covers Ada/Hopper.

Applies with `patch -p1` against any GCC 16 source tree.

--- a/gcc/config.gcc
+++ b/gcc/config.gcc
@@ -4233,7 +4233,7 @@
       with_arch=mips2
       ;;
     nvptx-*)
-      with_arch=sm_52
+      with_arch=sm_80
       ;;
   esac
 
@@ -5757,7 +5757,7 @@
 	nvptx-*)
 		supported_defaults=arch
 
-		nvptx_multilibs_default=sm_52
+		nvptx_multilibs_default=sm_89
 
 		case "x${with_multilib_list}" in
 		x | xno)
